{"kind":"report","text":"Initial forge and development-platform research is ready for feature discussion. No feature set, UI implementation, automation runtime or deployment execution is selected or authorized by this report. Research includes four parallel comparative/design investigations plus native automation and full-lifecycle follow-up prompted by Hugh's VS Code reference. It applies frontend-app-builder research/inventory guidance, transferable mobile navigation patterns, Tufte visualization guidance and current primary Git/GitHub/GitLab/Apple/W3C documentation. Comparative findings are documentation research, not hands-on product usability results.\n\nProduct direction: unify purpose, obligations and consequences of work. A person should follow issue/conditions → commitments/plans/concerns → reports/change version → review/check evidence → confirmed publication → potential deployment/observation without reconstructing identity or losing their place. This is a network of exact relationships, not a claim that all work proceeds in one linear order. Keep Git parent topology distinct from coordination relationships.\n\nCandidate capability map, for selection:\n1. Arrival/attention: rooms/repositories, work promised, requested reviews, blockers and continuation. Attention is a projection linking to canonical records, not another authority.\n2. Purpose/work: issue discussion, conditions, commitments, plans, concerns, reports and linked changes; assignment alone must not imply a promise.\n3. Source inspection: refs, railway history, commit details, full tree vs changed-file list, file history, scoped search/blame, stable permalinks, explicit comparisons, unified/split diffs and bounded large/binary/LFS/submodule states.\n4. Review/readiness: selected immutable version, anchored discussions, applicable requirements, qualifying reviews/jobs/results, replacements/interdiff, publication attempts/receipts.\n5. Automation: native admission guards, committed-event messages, authorized jobs, attempts/evidence, manual/scheduled triggers and provider integration as separately scoped contracts.\n6. Delivery/operation: built artifacts, previews, environments, promotion, provider operations, rollback compatibility and timestamped health/incident observations.\n7. Administration/integration: effective authority/rules, participants/controllers, sync progress/conflicts/revocation and recovery; browser editing and runnable development are distinct scope choices.\n\nFlow organizations to compare: (A) issue/purpose first, strong continuity but can overload an issue; (B) personal workbench first, good continuation across rooms but needs explainable attention/ranking; (C) repository/delivery first, strong source/operations orientation but risks separate silos. These can share canonical object pages and preserved navigation. A common action presentation should identify exact subject/version, current state, unmet requirements, available action and recorded result.\n\nDocumented comparative precedents: Tower explicitly separates changeset from historic full tree; GitLens embeds commit/diff/compare details with width-adaptive placement; GitLab exposes snapshot vs merge-base comparison intent. GitHub code search currently covers default-branch indexed code only and is not exhaustive. These support a proposed shared repository/ref/resolved-commit/path/comparison context with visible scope and completeness. Graph paging must retain actual ordered parent IDs and labelled continuation; a Git DAG is not an ARIA file tree. Mobile should preserve the same destinations in deliberate full-width flows, with keyboard/text ancestry alternatives, reliable Back/reload/permalinks, zoom and reduced-motion behavior.\n\nVerified current dap source: brand/tokens.css:3–21 and packages/page/src/index.html govern forest green/bone/ink, Open Runde/Teletype33/Sometype Mono, sharp surfaces and 8px module. Older 027 violet concepts are historical visual references; their one-home-per-fact and exact-version interaction principles remain useful. Main UI shell is packages/page/src/main.ts:418–443. directory.ts:163–184 and destination.ts:190–204 currently give one room one native repository/destination and one publication branch; multi-room/global workbench navigation remains a product decision. The verified Git reader supplies tree/parent/object foundations (reader.ts:32–87), not a paged forge query API. Current Page lists materialize lane state (data.ts:301–319). General graph/tree/diff/search backend contracts remain needed. Immutable public native-publication URLs already exist (docs/pages.md:23–39); they do not authorize arbitrary repository exploration.\n\nNative-platform audit: jobs already bind manifest/tree/configuration/deadline and qualified checker results. Stock request-check records a job but sends no runner request (change.ts:1025–1036). checkers service/runner explicitly lack a real deployed runner. Native guards, asynchronous verified messages and deadline alarms exist; arbitrary application external operations, a general scheduler and deployment effects remain missing contracts (docs/architecture.md:215–231; docs/roadmap.md:211–220). Plan020 proposed preview/build/promotion/rollback but is not delivery evidence. A pre-receive admission rule, post-event job and external deployment outcome have different semantics. A new check attempt, retry of an unknown operation and a new deployment must retain distinct identities.\n\nDeployment research: Cloudflare separates uploaded version from traffic deployment; KV/R2/DO/D1 state is not versioned with code. Promotion authority, exact artifact/configuration, provider reconciliation, concurrency, cancellation, secret custody, health-observer trust/freshness and state-compatible rollback need explicit contracts. Dap-native automation should be explored around meaningful collaboration facts as well as Git events, with provider runners supplying execution under explicit trust.\n\nValidation scenarios for later prototypes: resume an issue with several parallel changes; explain a merge and browse unchanged neighbouring code; compare exact versions and return to same selection; investigate a superseded failed check; find why publication is not confirmed; trace a running version to purpose/review/evidence; promote or recover without implying approval means execution. Include partial/missing history, force-push, merge-base ambiguity, deep/huge trees, binary/LFS/submodules, keyboard/screen-reader/touch/zoom, unknown outcomes and revoked authority.\n\nLimitation: current browser tool reports no available browser, so current source governs the visual baseline; no current live rendering or usability acceptance was claimed. No source changes, installs, tests or provider operations. Existing builder priorities and their delivery monitoring continue.\n\nPrimary references: https://www.git-tower.com/help/guides/commit-history/historic-file-trees/mac ; https://help.gitkraken.com/gitlens/gl-commit-graph/ ; https://docs.gitlab.com/user/project/repository/compare_revisions/ ; https://docs.github.com/en/search-github/github-code-search/about-github-code-search ; https://git-scm.com/docs/git-diff ; https://git-scm.com/docs/githooks ; https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/treeview/ ; https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/reflow.html ; https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/events-that-trigger-workflows ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/versions-and-deployments/ .\n"}